message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Verifying more is not enough when false positives track the environmental gradient in occupancy models"
abstract: >-
  Research compendium (fpcalib) for a simulation study of a Bayesian
  multiple-methods false-positive occupancy model fitted in Stan, compared
  with the frequentist occuFP estimator from unmarked. It simulates acoustic
  detection data under homogeneous, unstructured, and structured
  false-positive regimes with partial verification, scores the 95% interval
  coverage and bias of the occupancy slope, and tests whether modelling the
  false-positive rate as a function of site covariates restores calibration.
